# CBMC 5.5

This release includes full support for __attribute__((weak)) (weak ELF symbols)
(via #39), code contracts (via #26), and configuration support for HPPA and SH4
architectures (via #87). It also includes 87 further changes.

## What's Changed
* Full support for __attribute__((weak)) (weak ELF symbols) by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/39
* Code contracts by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/26
* Enum linking by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/24
* merge_irept should not destroy comments (but it may ignore differences) by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/32
* Slice with respect to select properties by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/21
* JSIL (Javscript Intermediate Language) front-end by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/51
* Handle missing arguments more gracefully by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/54
* Java bytecode: use expr2java instead of expr2c, formatting fix by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/56
* Dead-code analysis with plain text or json output by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/59
* Parse the __noreturn__ attribute by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/57
* Cleanup and beautification of json output by @tautschnig in https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/pull/60
